<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Itagaki Taisuke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1919</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Itagaki Taisuke was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> of the Tosa domain who commanded troops for the new imperial government in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boshin-war">Boshin War</a> of 1868–1869 and served in the early Meiji government. Leaving it in 1873 over a proposed expedition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, he led the Freedom and People's Rights Movement for an elected assembly and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s first national political party, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a>, in 1881.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/itagaki-taisuke.jpg" alt="Itagaki Taisuke" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Itagaki_Taisuke_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
